  "id": "multilevel-model",
  "term": "multilevel model",
  "definition": "A multilevel model is an integrative framework that explains a phenomenon by linking several interacting levels or domains rather than relying on a single mechanism. In this source, it refers to a unified account that connects psychological processes, identity-related factors, neurocognitive mechanisms, and clinical outcomes to show how they work together.",
